[31m-## Why use braces?[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Brace patterns make globs more powerful by adding the ability to match specific ranges and sequences of characters.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- **Accurate** - complete support for the [Bash 4.3 Brace Expansion](www.gnu.org/software/bash/) specification (passes all of the Bash braces tests)[m
[31m-- **[fast and performant](#benchmarks)** - Starts fast, runs fast and [scales well](#performance) as patterns increase in complexity.[m
[31m-- **Organized code base** - The parser and compiler are easy to maintain and update when edge cases crop up.[m
[31m-- **Well-tested** - Thousands of test assertions, and passes all of the Bash, minimatch, and [brace-expansion](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion) unit tests (as of the date this was written).[m
[31m-- **Safer** - You shouldn't have to worry about users defining aggressive or malicious brace patterns that can break your application. Braces takes measures to prevent malicious regex that can be used for DDoS attacks (see [catastrophic backtracking](https://www.regular-expressions.info/catastrophic.html)).[m
[31m-- [Supports lists](#lists) - (aka "sets") `a/{b,c}/d` => `['a/b/d', 'a/c/d']`[m
[31m-- [Supports sequences](#sequences) - (aka "ranges") `{01..03}` => `['01', '02', '03']`[m
[31m-- [Supports steps](#steps) - (aka "increments") `{2..10..2}` => `['2', '4', '6', '8', '10']`[m
[31m-- [Supports escaping](#escaping) - To prevent evaluation of special characters.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Usage[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The main export is a function that takes one or more brace `patterns` and `options`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-const braces = require('braces');[m
[31m-// braces(patterns[, options]);[m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces(['{01..05}', '{a..e}']));[m
[31m-//=> ['(0[1-5])', '([a-e])'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces(['{01..05}', '{a..e}'], { expand: true }));[m
[31m-//=> ['01', '02', '03', '04', '05', 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Brace Expansion vs. Compilation[m
[31m-[m
[31m-By default, brace patterns are compiled into strings that are optimized for creating regular expressions and matching.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Compiled**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{x,y,z}/b'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/(x|y|z)/b'][m
[31m-console.log(braces(['a/{01..20}/b', 'a/{1..5}/b']));[m
[31m-//=> [ 'a/(0[1-9]|1[0-9]|20)/b', 'a/([1-5])/b' ][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Expanded**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Enable brace expansion by setting the `expand` option to true, or by using [braces.expand()](#expand) (returns an array similar to what you'd expect from Bash, or `echo {1..5}`, or [minimatch](https://github.com/isaacs/minimatch)):[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{x,y,z}/b', { expand: true }));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/x/b', 'a/y/b', 'a/z/b'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('{01..10}'));[m
[31m-//=> ['01','02','03','04','05','06','07','08','09','10'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Lists[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Expand lists (like Bash "sets"):[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{foo,bar,baz}/*.js'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/(foo|bar|baz)/*.js'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a/{foo,bar,baz}/*.js'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/foo/*.js', 'a/bar/*.js', 'a/baz/*.js'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Sequences[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Expand ranges of characters (like Bash "sequences"):[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('{1..3}')); // ['1', '2', '3'][m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a/{1..3}/b')); // ['a/1/b', 'a/2/b', 'a/3/b'][m
[31m-console.log(braces('{a..c}', { expand: true })); // ['a', 'b', 'c'][m
[31m-console.log(braces('foo/{a..c}', { expand: true })); // ['foo/a', 'foo/b', 'foo/c'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-// supports zero-padded ranges[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{01..03}/b')); //=> ['a/(0[1-3])/b'][m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{001..300}/b')); //=> ['a/(0{2}[1-9]|0[1-9][0-9]|[12][0-9]{2}|300)/b'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-See [fill-range](https://github.com/jonschlinkert/fill-range) for all available range-expansion options.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Steppped ranges[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Steps, or increments, may be used with ranges:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('{2..10..2}'));[m
[31m-//=> ['2', '4', '6', '8', '10'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces('{2..10..2}'));[m
[31m-//=> ['(2|4|6|8|10)'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-When the [.optimize](#optimize) method is used, or [options.optimize](#optionsoptimize) is set to true, sequences are passed to [to-regex-range](https://github.com/jonschlinkert/to-regex-range) for expansion.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Nesting[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Brace patterns may be nested. The results of each expanded string are not sorted, and left to right order is preserved.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**"Expanded" braces**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a{b,c,/{x,y}}/e'));[m
[31m-//=> ['ab/e', 'ac/e', 'a/x/e', 'a/y/e'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a/{x,{1..5},y}/c'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/x/c', 'a/1/c', 'a/2/c', 'a/3/c', 'a/4/c', 'a/5/c', 'a/y/c'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**"Optimized" braces**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a{b,c,/{x,y}}/e'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a(b|c|/(x|y))/e'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{x,{1..5},y}/c'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a/(x|([1-5])|y)/c'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Escaping[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Escaping braces**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A brace pattern will not be expanded or evaluted if _either the opening or closing brace is escaped_:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a\\{d,c,b}e'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a{d,c,b}e'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a{d,c,b\\}e'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a{d,c,b}e'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Escaping commas**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Commas inside braces may also be escaped:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a{b\\,c}d'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a{b,c}d'][m
[31m-[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a{d\\,c,b}e'));[m
[31m-//=> ['ad,ce', 'abe'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Single items**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Following bash conventions, a brace pattern is also not expanded when it contains a single character:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces.expand('a{b}c'));[m
[31m-//=> ['a{b}c'][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Options[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### options.maxLength[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Type**: `Number`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Default**: `10,000`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Description**: Limit the length of the input string. Useful when the input string is generated or your application allows users to pass a string, et cetera.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{b,c}/d', { maxLength: 3 })); //=> throws an error[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### options.expand[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Type**: `Boolean`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Default**: `undefined`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Description**: Generate an "expanded" brace pattern (alternatively you can use the `braces.expand()` method, which does the same thing).[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```js[m
[31m-console.log(braces('a/{b,c}/d', { expand: true }));[m
[31m-//=> [ 'a/b/d', 'a/c/d' ][m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### options.nodupes[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Type**: `Boolean`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Default**: `undefined`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Description**: Remove duplicates from the returned array.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### options.rangeLimit[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Type**: `Number`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Default**: `1000`[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Description**: To prevent malicious patterns from being passed by users, an error is thrown when `braces.expand()` is used or `options.expand` is true and the generated range will exceed the `rangeLimit`.[m
