[31m-# minimatch[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A minimal matching utility.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-This is the matching library used internally by npm.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-It works by converting glob expressions into JavaScript `RegExp`[m
[31m-objects.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Important Security Consideration![m
[31m-[m
[31m-> [!WARNING]  [m
[31m-> This library uses JavaScript regular expressions. Please read[m
[31m-> the following warning carefully, and be thoughtful about what[m
[31m-> you provide to this library in production systems.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-_Any_ library in JavaScript that deals with matching string[m
[31m-patterns using regular expressions will be subject to[m
[31m-[ReDoS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS)[m
[31m-if the pattern is generated using untrusted input.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Efforts have been made to mitigate risk as much as is feasible in[m
[31m-such a library, providing maximum recursion depths and so forth,[m
[31m-but these measures can only ultimately protect against accidents,[m
[31m-not malice. A dedicated attacker can _always_ find patterns that[m
[31m-cannot be defended against by a bash-compatible glob pattern[m
[31m-matching system that uses JavaScript regular expressions.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-To be extremely clear:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-> [!WARNING]  [m
[31m-> **If you create a system where you take user input, and use[m
[31m-> that input as the source of a Regular Expression pattern, in[m
[31m-> this or any extant glob matcher in JavaScript, you will be[m
[31m-> pwned.**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A future version of this library _may_ use a different matching[m
[31m-algorithm which does not exhibit backtracking problems. If and[m
[31m-when that happens, it will likely be a sweeping change, and those[m
[31m-improvements will **not** be backported to legacy versions.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-In the near term, it is not reasonable to continue to play[m
[31m-whack-a-mole with security advisories, and so any future ReDoS[m
[31m-reports will be considered "working as intended", and resolved[m
[31m-entirely by this warning.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Usage[m
