[31m-## Minimatch Class[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Create a minimatch object by instantiating the `minimatch.Minimatch` class.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```javascript[m
[31m-var Minimatch = require('minimatch').Minimatch[m
[31m-var mm = new Minimatch(pattern, options)[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Properties[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `pattern` The original pattern the minimatch object represents.[m
[31m-- `options` The options supplied to the constructor.[m
[31m-- `set` A 2-dimensional array of regexp or string expressions.[m
[31m-  Each row in the[m
[31m-  array corresponds to a brace-expanded pattern. Each item in the row[m
[31m-  corresponds to a single path-part. For example, the pattern[m
[31m-  `{a,b/c}/d` would expand to a set of patterns like:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-        [ [ a, d ][m
[31m-        , [ b, c, d ] ][m
[31m-[m
[31m-  If a portion of the pattern doesn't have any "magic" in it[m
[31m-  (that is, it's something like `"foo"` rather than `fo*o?`), then it[m
[31m-  will be left as a string rather than converted to a regular[m
[31m-  expression.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `regexp` Created by the `makeRe` method. A single regular expression[m
[31m-  expressing the entire pattern. This is useful in cases where you wish[m
[31m-  to use the pattern somewhat like `fnmatch(3)` with `FNM_PATH` enabled.[m
[31m-- `negate` True if the pattern is negated.[m
[31m-- `comment` True if the pattern is a comment.[m
[31m-- `empty` True if the pattern is `""`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Methods[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `makeRe()` Generate the `regexp` member if necessary, and return it.[m
[31m-  Will return `false` if the pattern is invalid.[m
[31m-- `match(fname)` Return true if the filename matches the pattern, or[m
[31m-  false otherwise.[m
[31m-- `matchOne(fileArray, patternArray, partial)` Take a `/`-split[m
[31m-  filename, and match it against a single row in the `regExpSet`. This[m
[31m-  method is mainly for internal use, but is exposed so that it can be[m
[31m-  used by a glob-walker that needs to avoid excessive filesystem calls.[m
[31m-- `hasMagic()` Returns true if the parsed pattern contains any[m
[31m-  magic characters. Returns false if all comparator parts are[m
[31m-  string literals. If the `magicalBraces` option is set on the[m
[31m-  constructor, then it will consider brace expansions which are[m
[31m-  not otherwise magical to be magic. If not set, then a pattern[m
[31m-  like `a{b,c}d` will return `false`, because neither `abd` nor[m
[31m-  `acd` contain any special glob characters.[m
[31m-[m
