[31m-## Conventions[m
[31m-[m
[31m-If you're using this in one or more of your libraries, you _should_ use the name of your library so that developers may toggle debugging as desired without guessing names. If you have more than one debuggers you _should_ prefix them with your library name and use ":" to separate features. For example "bodyParser" from Connect would then be "connect:bodyParser".  If you append a "*" to the end of your name, it will always be enabled regardless of the setting of the DEBUG environment variable.  You can then use it for normal output as well as debug output.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Wildcards[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The `*` character may be used as a wildcard. Suppose for example your library has[m
[31m-debuggers named "connect:bodyParser", "connect:compress", "connect:session",[m
[31m-instead of listing all three with[m
[31m-`DEBUG=connect:bodyParser,connect:compress,connect:session`, you may simply do[m
[31m-`DEBUG=connect:*`, or to run everything using this module simply use `DEBUG=*`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-You can also exclude specific debuggers by prefixing them with a "-" character.[m
[31m-For example, `DEBUG=*,-connect:*` would include all debuggers except those[m
[31m-starting with "connect:".[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Environment Variables[m
[31m-[m
[31m-When running through Node.js, you can set a few environment variables that will[m
[31m-change the behavior of the debug logging:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Name      | Purpose                                         |[m
[31m-|-----------|-------------------------------------------------|[m
[31m-| `DEBUG`   | Enables/disables specific debugging namespaces. |[m
[31m-| `DEBUG_HIDE_DATE` | Hide date from debug output (non-TTY).  |[m
[31m-| `DEBUG_COLORS`| Whether or not to use colors in the debug output. |[m
[31m-| `DEBUG_DEPTH` | Object inspection depth.                    |[m
[31m-| `DEBUG_SHOW_HIDDEN` | Shows hidden properties on inspected objects. |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-__Note:__ The environment variables beginning with `DEBUG_` end up being[m
[31m-converted into an Options object that gets used with `%o`/`%O` formatters.[m
[31m-See the Node.js documentation for[m
[31m-[`util.inspect()`](https://nodejs.org/api/util.html#util_util_inspect_object_options)[m
[31m-for the complete list.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Formatters[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Debug uses [printf-style](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Printf_format_string) formatting.[m
[31m-Below are the officially supported formatters:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Formatter | Representation |[m
[31m-|-----------|----------------|[m
[31m-| `%O`      | Pretty-print an Object on multiple lines. |[m
[31m-| `%o`      | Pretty-print an Object all on a single line. |[m
[31m-| `%s`      | String. |[m
[31m-| `%d`      | Number (both integer and float). |[m
