[31m-## Usage in child processes[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Due to the way `debug` detects if the output is a TTY or not, colors are not shown in child processes when `stderr` is piped. A solution is to pass the `DEBUG_COLORS=1` environment variable to the child process.  [m
[31m-For example:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```javascript[m
[31m-worker = fork(WORKER_WRAP_PATH, [workerPath], {[m
[31m-  stdio: [[m
[31m-    /* stdin: */ 0,[m
[31m-    /* stdout: */ 'pipe',[m
[31m-    /* stderr: */ 'pipe',[m
[31m-    'ipc',[m
[31m-  ],[m
[31m-  env: Object.assign({}, process.env, {[m
[31m-    DEBUG_COLORS: 1 // without this settings, colors won't be shown[m
[31m-  }),[m
[31m-});[m
[31m-[m
[31m-worker.stderr.pipe(process.stderr, { end: false });[m
[31m-```[m
