[31m-## API[m
[31m-[m
[31m-`const stream = readdirp(root[, options])` — **Stream API**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Reads given root recursively and returns a `stream` of [entry infos](#entryinfo)[m
[31m-- Optionally can be used like `for await (const entry of stream)` with node.js 10+ (`asyncIterator`).[m
[31m-- `on('data', (entry) => {})` [entry info](#entryinfo) for every file / dir.[m
[31m-- `on('warn', (error) => {})` non-fatal `Error` that prevents a file / dir from being processed. Example: inaccessible to the user.[m
[31m-- `on('error', (error) => {})` fatal `Error` which also ends the stream. Example: illegal options where passed.[m
[31m-- `on('end')` — we are done. Called when all entries were found and no more will be emitted.[m
[31m-- `on('close')` — stream is destroyed via `stream.destroy()`.[m
[31m-  Could be useful if you want to manually abort even on a non fatal error.[m
[31m-  At that point the stream is no longer `readable` and no more entries, warning or errors are emitted[m
[31m-- To learn more about streams, consult the very detailed [nodejs streams documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html)[m
