[31m-## Versions[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A "version" is described by the `v2.0.0` specification found at[m
[31m-<https://semver.org/>.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A leading `"="` or `"v"` character is stripped off and ignored.[m
[31m-Support for stripping a leading "v" is kept for compatibility with `v1.0.0` of the SemVer[m
[31m-specification but should not be used anymore.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Ranges[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A `version range` is a set of `comparators` that specify versions[m
[31m-that satisfy the range.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A `comparator` is composed of an `operator` and a `version`.  The set[m
[31m-of primitive `operators` is:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-* `<` Less than[m
[31m-* `<=` Less than or equal to[m
[31m-* `>` Greater than[m
[31m-* `>=` Greater than or equal to[m
[31m-* `=` Equal.  If no operator is specified, then equality is assumed,[m
[31m-  so this operator is optional but MAY be included.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-For example, the comparator `>=1.2.7` would match the versions[m
[31m-`1.2.7`, `1.2.8`, `2.5.3`, and `1.3.9`, but not the versions `1.2.6`[m
[31m-or `1.1.0`. The comparator `>1` is equivalent to `>=2.0.0` and[m
[31m-would match the versions `2.0.0` and `3.1.0`, but not the versions[m
[31m-`1.0.1` or `1.1.0`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Comparators can be joined by whitespace to form a `comparator set`,[m
[31m-which is satisfied by the **intersection** of all of the comparators[m
[31m-it includes.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A range is composed of one or more comparator sets, joined by `||`.  A[m
[31m-version matches a range if and only if every comparator in at least[m
[31m-one of the `||`-separated comparator sets is satisfied by the version.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-For example, the range `>=1.2.7 <1.3.0` would match the versions[m
[31m-`1.2.7`, `1.2.8`, and `1.2.99`, but not the versions `1.2.6`, `1.3.0`,[m
[31m-or `1.1.0`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The range `1.2.7 || >=1.2.9 <2.0.0` would match the versions `1.2.7`,[m
[31m-`1.2.9`, and `1.4.6`, but not the versions `1.2.8` or `2.0.0`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Prerelease Tags[m
[31m-[m
[31m-If a version has a prerelease tag (for example, `1.2.3-alpha.3`) then[m
[31m-it will only be allowed to satisfy comparator sets if at least one[m
[31m-comparator with the same `[major, minor, patch]` tuple also has a[m
[31m-prerelease tag.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-For example, the range `>1.2.3-alpha.3` would be allowed to match the[m
[31m-version `1.2.3-alpha.7`, but it would *not* be satisfied by[m
[31m-`3.4.5-alpha.9`, even though `3.4.5-alpha.9` is technically "greater[m
[31m-than" `1.2.3-alpha.3` according to the SemVer sort rules.  The version[m
[31m-range only accepts prerelease tags on the `1.2.3` version.[m
[31m-Version `3.4.5` *would* satisfy the range because it does not have a[m
[31m-prerelease flag, and `3.4.5` is greater than `1.2.3-alpha.7`.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The purpose of this behavior is twofold.  First, prerelease versions[m
[31m-frequently are updated very quickly, and contain many breaking changes[m
[31m-that are (by the author's design) not yet fit for public consumption.[m
[31m-Therefore, by default, they are excluded from range-matching[m
[31m-semantics.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Second, a user who has opted into using a prerelease version has[m
[31m-indicated the intent to use *that specific* set of[m
[31m-alpha/beta/rc versions.  By including a prerelease tag in the range,[m
[31m-the user is indicating that they are aware of the risk.  However, it[m
[31m-is still not appropriate to assume that they have opted into taking a[m
[31m-similar risk on the *next* set of prerelease versions.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Note that this behavior can be suppressed (treating all prerelease[m
[31m-versions as if they were normal versions, for range-matching)[m
[31m-by setting the `includePrerelease` flag on the options[m
[31m-object to any[m
[31m-[functions](https://github.com/npm/node-semver#functions) that do[m
[31m-range matching.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-#### Prerelease Identifiers[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The method `.inc` takes an additional `identifier` string argument that[m
[31m-will append the value of the string as a prerelease identifier:[m
