[31m-<br>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-</details>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<details>[m
[31m-<summary><strong>Why use this library?</strong></summary>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<br>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Convenience[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Creating regular expressions for matching numbers gets deceptively complicated pretty fast.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-For example, let's say you need a validation regex for matching part of a user-id, postal code, social security number, tax id, etc:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` => `/1/` (easy enough)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` through `5` => `/[1-5]/` (not bad...)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` or `5` => `/(1|5)/` (still easy...)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` through `50` => `/([1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|50)/` (uh-oh...)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` through `55` => `/([1-9]|[1-4][0-9]|5[0-5])/` (no prob, I can do this...)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `1` through `555` => `/([1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|[1-4][0-9]{2}|5[0-4][0-9]|55[0-5])/` (maybe not...)[m
[31m-* regex for matching `0001` through `5555` => `/(0{3}[1-9]|0{2}[1-9][0-9]|0[1-9][0-9]{2}|[1-4][0-9]{3}|5[0-4][0-9]{2}|55[0-4][0-9]|555[0-5])/` (okay, I get the point!)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The numbers are contrived, but they're also really basic. In the real world you might need to generate a regex on-the-fly for validation.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Learn more**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-If you're interested in learning more about [character classes](http://www.regular-expressions.info/charclass.html) and other regex features, I personally have always found [regular-expressions.info](http://www.regular-expressions.info/charclass.html) to be pretty useful.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Heavily tested[m
[31m-[m
[31m-As of April 07, 2019, this library runs [>1m test assertions](./test/test.js) against generated regex-ranges to provide brute-force verification that results are correct.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Tests run in ~280ms on my MacBook Pro, 2.5 GHz Intel Core i7.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Optimized[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Generated regular expressions are optimized:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-* duplicate sequences and character classes are reduced using quantifiers[m
[31m-* smart enough to use `?` conditionals when number(s) or range(s) can be positive or negative[m
[31m-* uses fragment caching to avoid processing the same exact string more than once[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<br>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-</details>[m
